    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:12Z",
      "text": "Bahrain is an island country in the eastern part of the Arabian Peninsula in West Asia, officially known as the Kingdom of Bahrain.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386535988:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "On 13 November Iran said it destroyed a Bahraini early-warning radar in retaliation for a US strike on Sirik, and on 14 November it attacked an American base there with drones and missiles.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-13:1",
        "wiki:2026-11-14:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:34Z",
      "text": "On 16 November, Bahrain sentenced 64 Shia Muslims, mostly clerics, to life in prison for establishing a terrorist group linked to Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:00:43Z",
      "text": "On 17 November, Bahrain's military intercepted a number of drones fired by Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps at Sheikh Isa Air Base.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-17:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:01:01Z",
      "text": "France 24 headlined its coverage \"Middle East live: Kuwait, Bahrain report drone and missile attacks.\"",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:e3338d2d36dc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-18T00:01:07Z",
      "text": "BBC News headlined its report \"Kuwait says it repelled first Iranian attack in two months after US strikes island.\"",
      "cites": [
